      ":question/id": "924f4c34-6cb8-5c89-9f0f-9602f5e91c27",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "If $f(x)=\\frac{2 \\tan{\\left(x \\right)}}{x}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x)$ wherever the original quotient is defined.\n\n$f^{\\prime}(x)=$ {{field-1}}.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=2 \\tan{\\left(x \\right)}$ and $v(x)=x.$\n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}(x)&=\\frac{u^{\\prime}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot v^{\\prime}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(2 \\tan{\\left(x \\right)})^{\\prime}\\cdot (x)-(2 \\tan{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (x)^{\\prime}}{(x)^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{2\\sec^2 x\\cdot x-2\\tan x\\cdot 1}{x^2}\\\\ &=\\frac{2x\\sec^2 x-2\\tan x}{x^2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "3100fcbc-4412-5184-b374-102279e8fbc1",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "dfd61a7e-807d-5906-af61-fe704113ceb6",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{2 \\left(x \\tan^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + x - \\tan{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)}{x^{2}}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
